# edp-migrate's own config — what its Setup wizard prefills before
# anything's been saved (internal/config/config.go's DefaultLocalConfig,
# since v0.2.3 — see the core tool's own README.md "Setup wizard port
# defaults" section for the full env-var reference).
#
# edp-migrate runs as its own container on this same "tyk" docker
# network — so it reaches every other service directly by its real
# internal service name, paired with that service's real internal port
# (always 3000/3001/5432/6379, regardless of whatever host-side port
# each one is actually published as in .env). This is a direct route
# that doesn't depend on any host-port mapping at all — no separate sync
# mechanism needed, and nothing here ever needs to change even if this
# stack's own *_HOST_PORT values do.
EDP_MIGRATE_DASHBOARD_HOST=tyk-dashboard
EDP_MIGRATE_DASHBOARD_PORT=3000
EDP_MIGRATE_PORTAL_HOST=tyk-ent-portal
EDP_MIGRATE_PORTAL_PORT=3001
EDP_MIGRATE_POSTGRES_HOST=tyk-postgres
EDP_MIGRATE_POSTGRES_PORT=5432
EDP_MIGRATE_REDIS_HOST=tyk-redis
EDP_MIGRATE_REDIS_PORT=6379

# EDP_MIGRATE_HOST (a blanket fallback for any component whose own
# *_HOST var isn't set) is deliberately left unset here — every component
# edp-migrate talks to in this stack already has its own explicit
# internal-docker-name override above, so there's nothing left for a
# blanket fallback to apply to. It's there in the core tool for a
# component that ISN'T part of this docker network at all (e.g.
# host.docker.internal, to reach something running on the host machine
# instead) — set it yourself if you ever need that.

# Every category of operation, always to stderr — see the core tool's own
# README.md "Logging" section. debug is a reasonable default while
# actively testing against this stack; drop to info for quieter output.
EDP_MIGRATE_LOG_LEVEL=debug
EDP_MIGRATE_LOG_FORMAT=text
